# Defense in depth for the Vercel deploy: with the static export dropped,
# everything under public/ is served as-is. Under public/captures/ the ONLY thing
# published is the content-addressed screenshot PNGs — expressed as an allowlist so
# it is leak-proof by default: the capture JSON, working files, raw accessibility
# snapshots, secrets, and OS/editor cruft stay out regardless of git state, and a
# NEW stray file type is excluded unless it is explicitly allowed below. (Replaces
# scripts/prune-export.ts, which kept the same allowlist on the old static export;
# a denylist would silently ship whatever it forgot to list.)
#
# The capture JSON is no longer served from here at all: index.json is published at
# /index.json, and app.json / graph.json / view.json through /apps/... route
# handlers that bake the bytes into the build output (force-static). So only the
# PNGs need re-including below.

# Ignore everything under captures, but keep descending into subdirectories so
# the re-include below can reach nested files.
/public/captures/**
!/public/captures/**/
# Re-include only the published screenshot PNGs.
!/public/captures/**/*.png
# _staging is never published — drop its whole subtree even though it holds PNGs.
/public/captures/**/_staging/

# Secrets anywhere in the repo (belt-and-suspenders; also covers non-capture paths).
**/credentials.md
**/*.pem
.env*.local
